{
  "about": "The console lines of a logger, which Go's records/console handler, the Bun logger and the Python handler each write byte for byte. at is unix nanoseconds as text; level is slog's number, absent for an event; context and attrs are [key, value] pairs, a value as JSON writes it. redact names the secrets a key's words hide, and redact_secrets adds secrets, the list each language exports; a URL's password is hidden unless keep_url_passwords is true. pretty is in UTC, coloured when color is true, its time clock, full or off as time says and without the stream when hide_stream is true, which leave json as it is; a source shows as its directory, file and line. go test ./records/console -run TestConsoleLinesAreTheVectors -update writes json and pretty from Go's.",
